2026-11-19 03:39:15 - Agent_20261119033811 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed both CodeQL results for py/jinja2-unsafe-deserialization in src/jinja2/bccache.py plus surrounding cache infrastructure (FileSystemBytecodeCache, MemcachedBytecodeCache, BytecodeCache.get_bucket).

Submitted 3 findings:
1. TP — src/jinja2/bccache.py:71 `pickle.load(f)` in Bucket.load_bytecode. Only guard is the static bc_magic prefix, trivially forgeable; cache files are opened with plain open() in FileSystemBytecodeCache.load_bytecode. Arbitrary code execution via pickle gadgets.
2. MR — src/jinja2/bccache.py:77 `marshal.load(f)` loading an arbitrary CodeType object that Jinja later executes as compiled template bytecode; sandbox-escape potential, medium confidence.
3. TP (new, discovered independently) — src/jinja2/bccache.py:391 MemcachedBytecodeCache.load_bytecode passes the memcached get() value straight into bucket.bytecode_from_string, making Bucket.bytecode_from_string a remote untrusted deserialization sink. ignore_memcache_errors only wraps client.get, not deserialization, so cache poisoning of memcached yields RCE in the host process.

Root cause across all: bc_magic is an unkeyed static prefix mistaken for integrity validation, and there is no HMAC/signature over cache payloads.
